  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene07> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l5-f-distribution> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene07> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l6-df> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene07> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/SceneDefinition> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene07> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene07> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/focusConcept> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-one-way-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene07> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-item-07-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene07> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-item-07-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene07> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene07> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-package> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene07> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-scipy-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene07> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/narration> "These illustrative synthetic measurements represent eighteen independent river-water sample preparations, six for each SPE method. Recovery is recorded as a percentage, not as a fraction. Each method has its own mean: 94%, 98% and 93% for A, B and C. The grand mean is 95%, calculated over all eighteen preparations. Equal group sizes make this also the average of the three group means; unequal sizes would require weighting. Use the view control to inspect the different references for departures. Between-group and within-group scaling create explicitly hypothetical states, not new measurements. Differences use percentage points and squared departures use percentage points squared. Classical inference assumes independent Normal errors with a common positive variance. An omnibus comparison concerns all population means jointly, not individual pairwise conclusions."@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene13> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l5-f-distribution> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene13> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l6-df> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene13> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/SceneDefinition> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene13> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene13> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/focusConcept> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-one-way-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene13> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-item-13-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene13> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-item-13-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene13> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-item-13-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene13> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene13> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-package> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene13> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-scipy-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene13> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/narration> "Start with the illustrative synthetic river-water preparations and keep each observation attached to its original method. The between-group scale moves group means relative to the grand mean, while the within-group scale changes departures around each group mean. These are hypothetical teaching transformations, not laboratory observations. Reset restores the original percentages. Inspect how the ratio of between-group to within-group mean squares changes rather than assuming that a larger spread always strengthens evidence. Both mean squares use percentage points squared, so their ratio is dimensionless. The displayed formula and attached symbol legend describe this comparison. A zero within-group mean square is a degenerate state, not an ordinary zero statistic. Classical calibration assumes independent Normal errors with common positive variance. The omnibus result does not identify which pairs of population means differ."@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene19> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l5-f-distribution> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene19> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/references> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l6-df> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene19> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/SceneDefinition> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene19> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/authoredResource> "true"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene19> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/focusConcept> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-one-way-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene19> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-item-19-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene19> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSceneItem> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-item-19-2> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene19> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene19> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-package> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene19> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/hasSource> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-scipy-anova> .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-scene19> <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/ontology/narration> "For the original illustrative synthetic river-water preparations, F = 21 with degrees of freedom 2 and 15. The upper-tail probability is p = 0.0000448356040690602 under equal population means. At a prespecified significance level of 0.05, this rejects that joint null, assuming independent Normal errors with common positive variance. This is not the probability that the null is true and does not identify differing pairs. Recovery is in percent; differences are percentage points. Scale controls create hypothetical observations requiring recomputed statistics; baseline numbers do not describe transformed states. The initial view uses the existing generic F-reference panel with density, an F marker and visible tail shading, not a separately authored drawing. Display bounds omit infinity, but the analytic probability counts the full right tail."@en .
}

<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/sources/level7-anova-probe> {
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "NIST/SEMATECH" .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Methods reference for one-way analysis of variance; not the provenance of the synthetic observations."@en .
  <https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/resource/l7-source-nist-anova> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/identifier> "NIST-PPC-2.3.1" .
